From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 13 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] client: do not decode content-encoding on a 206 partial
 response

`fetch` picks a Gzip/Brotli/Zlib/Zstd decoder from the response's
Content-Encoding and wraps the body in it for every response that has one.
A `206 Partial Content` body is not a whole coded stream, though: the
origin computes the byte range over the *compressed* representation (the
Content-Range denominator is the compressed length), so the body is a
fragment of the gzip/brotli/zstd stream. Running a decoder over a fragment
ends the stream with `UnexpectedEof` (the read errors part way), or, when
the cut lands on a block boundary, decodes to a short, truncated body with
no error at all. A truncated font delivered to the page then fails Chrome's
OTS sanitizer with "Size of decompressed WOFF 2.0 is less than compressed
size", and any ranged, content-encoded resource (media, large assets) is
corrupted the same way.

A proxy cannot decode a partial coded stream and must not try: leave a
partial response encoded, headers untouched, and let the real client decode
the range it asked for (a service worker response is not re-decoded by the
browser from Content-Encoding, and a direct range consumer handles the
coding itself). Detect the partial response by its 206 status or the
presence of a Content-Range header and force the decoder off for it.
---
 client/src/lib.rs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/client/src/lib.rs b/client/src/lib.rs
index a1b2c3d..e4f5a6b 100644
--- a/client/src/lib.rs
+++ b/client/src/lib.rs
@@ -783,6 +783,23 @@ impl EpoxyClient {
 						"zstd" => Some(EpoxyCompression::Zstd),
 						_ => None,
 					};
+
+					// A 206 Partial Content body is a fragment of the
+					// *content-coded* representation: the origin computes the
+					// range over the compressed bytes (the Content-Range
+					// denominator is the compressed length). A Gzip/Brotli/
+					// Zlib/Zstd decoder run over that fragment ends in
+					// UnexpectedEof, or decodes to a short, truncated body -- a
+					// truncated font then fails OTS with "Size of decompressed
+					// WOFF 2.0 is less than compressed size". Leave a partial
+					// response encoded and let the client decode the range.
+					let compression = if response.status().as_u16() == 206
+						|| response.headers().contains_key("Content-Range")
+					{
+						None
+					} else {
+						compression
+					};

 					let response_body = BodyDataStream::new(response.into_body()).map_err(std::io::Error::other).into_async_read();
 					let decompressed_body = match compression {
